{"segs": ["PA_ja_205:0.1"], "en": "The Jātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_205:0.2", "PA_ja_205:0.3"], "en": "The Second Book of Birth Stories (Dukanipāta), Chapter on the Nataṃdaḷha Group (Nataṃdaḷhavagga)", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_205:0.4"], "en": "5. The Gaṅgeyya Jātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_205:1.1", "PA_ja_205:1.2"], "en": "“The fish of the Gaṅgā is beautiful, and so too is that of the Yamunā;”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_205:1.3"], "en": "This man has four limbs,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_205:1.4"], "en": "his body is well-proportioned like a banyan tree,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_205:1.5"], "en": "and his neck is slightly curved.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_205:1.6"], "en": "He outshines them all.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_205:2.1", "PA_ja_205:2.2"], "en": "“What was asked, you did not explain; instead, when asked, you explained something else.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_205:2.3"], "en": "“A person who praises themselves—", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_205:2.4"], "en": "this is not pleasing to us.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_205:3.1"], "en": "The Gaṅgeyya Jātaka, the fifth.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"}
]
